		"In this course, students will explore environmental connections by looking deeply into natural systems, social systems, and the links between them using both quantitative and qualitative frameworks. Through this integrated approach, students will learn to analyze complex environmental challenges and identify solutions aimed at optimizing the health of people, animals, and ecosystems. Prerequisites: ENVST 137 or permission of instructor."
